The C++ rules engine and observation/deployment code adapt the official
Kaggle kaggle-environments Kaggriculture interpreter. These translations and
local modifications are covered by Apache-2.0; see LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt.
Upstream: https://github.com/Kaggle/kaggle-environments
Reference distribution: kaggle-environments 1.32.7.

Native bindings use pybind11 (BSD-3-Clause); its license is in LICENSES/.
Distributed native submission binaries statically link GCC runtime libraries.
The GCC Runtime Library Exception permits eligible applications to be distributed
under their own terms; the runtime retains its original license and exception.
See LICENSES/GPL-3.0.txt and LICENSES/GCC-Runtime-Library-Exception-3.1.txt.

Public notebook adaptations and route assets retain their Apache-2.0 licenses
and original attribution under src/kagg_revue/opponents/{kaito,boatlee,mugundh,
portfolios}/. Their original authors are credited in those NOTICE.md files.
Generated C++ adaptations remain covered by the corresponding upstream terms.
The source identities in portfolios/catalog.py identify the exact adaptations.

This distribution removes local machine paths and private service links.
It includes no historical Git author metadata, credentials, raw replay datasets,
or training checkpoint collection. Release archives describe their own changes
in release-provenance.json; original submitted archives remain unchanged.
